      "content": "Flickery permissions, especially when you've checked the IAM role, can sometimes be trickier than a straight-up \"No Access\" error. It's less likely to be the policy itself, as that's usually a consistent failure, but rather something external causing a temporary hiccup. You might be running into a race condition or a propagation delay, which can be frustratingly inconsistent, especially when dealing with cloud infrastructure. It's a good idea to check the AWS CloudTrail logs for the specific API call failures to see *exactly* what AWS is reporting at the moment the error occurs. This detailed log will often point to whether the issue is IAM, Bucket Policy, or something else entirely.",
